-- 244: the terms read the way they were written.
--
-- Kevin: "i didnt like how the quotation notes from francois rendered in odoo
-- they used to be rich text and there was a table also that lost its format".
-- He is right, and twice over. Odoo held these notes as HTML. 219 brought them
-- in as the plain text a textarea holds, so every heading lost its weight and
-- every cell of the payment schedule landed on its own line. 222 converted the
-- same source again so a row stayed on one line with " | " between the cells,
-- which the printed page could read back as a table; the form and the emailed
-- copy still showed the pipes.
--
-- The terms are rich text now, so the SAME SOURCE is converted a third and last
-- time, into the real thing: headings as headings, the schedule as a table, the
-- defined terms bold. Nothing is summarised, cut or reworded. What the customer
-- read in Odoo is what prints out of Orbit.
--
-- Written by supabase/odoo-notes-to-rich-text.pl from
-- odoo-to-orbit/notes-pull/odoo-notes-templates.json, pulled live on 10 Oct 2026.
-- That script follows rtClean's rules in js/app.js tag for tag, and
-- tests/richtext-import.html proves it: it runs the app's own sanitiser
-- over every string below and requires it back unchanged.
--
-- Two unnumbered Odoo drafts are skipped, because 210 deliberately did not import
-- them and there is nothing for them to land on. INV/2026/00002 is written below
-- and matches no row either: the notes were pulled on 10 Oct 2026, two months
-- after the 10 Aug export that 210 was built from, and that invoice was raised in
-- Odoo in between. Its terms were one line, a link to spacework.ai/terms. Run of
-- 6 Nov 2026: 4 templates, 14 sales orders and 8 invoices updated, none left
-- holding plain text.
--
-- Chunked because the Management API answers 400 with an EMPTY body to a
-- statement this long, which looks exactly like a SQL error and is not one.

-- @chunk

-- template: Facade Architectural Services
update public.quote_templates set note = '<p><strong>SPACEWORK SARL</strong> (hereinafter referred to as “SPACEWORK”), a company duly registered under the laws of Lebanon, with its principal place of business located at Beirut, specializing in façade consulting, engineering, and design; </p><p><strong>1. Scope of Work</strong> </p><p>SPACEWORK agrees to provide the following services to the Client: </p><p>1.1. Façade architectural basis of design, including: </p><p class="rt-in1">a. Façade concept drawings. </p><p class="rt-in1">b. Project specifications. </p><p>1.2. Consulting and engineering services related to façade design.</p><p><strong>2. Deliverables</strong> </p><p>2.1. General façade concept drawings reflecting the agreed-upon design approach. </p><p>2.2. Comprehensive project specifications outlining material requirements, performance criteria, testing, and other relevant details. </p><p><strong>3. Responsibilities of the Client</strong> </p><p>3.1. Provide SPACEWORK with all relevant project details, including architectural plans, project scope, timelines, and specific requirements.</p><p>3.2. Ensure timely communication and feedback to facilitate smooth project execution. </p><p>3.3. Obtain necessary approvals and permits for project execution, if required.</p><p><strong>4. Timeline</strong> </p><p>4.1. SPACEWORK will provide the agreed deliverables within specified time frame from the date of receiving all necessary project information from the Client. </p><p>4.2. Delays caused by the Client’s failure to provide required information or feedback will result in corresponding adjustments to the timeline, and may result in additional charges if the delay exceeds thirty calendar days.</p><p><strong>5. Fees and Payment Terms</strong> </p><p>5.1. The total fee for the services provided under this Agreement is mentioned above and should be settled in U.S.D Cash or USD Fresh Bank Transfer, exclusive of applicable taxes and transfer fees. </p><p>5.2. Payment milestones are as follows: </p><p class="rt-in1">a. 25% upon signing this Agreement. </p><p class="rt-in1">b. 25% upon submission of Materials and systems</p><p class="rt-in1">c. 20% upon submission of specifications</p><p class="rt-in1">d. 20% upon submission of Facade General Drawings</p><p class="rt-in1">e. 10% Remaining balance upon delivery of final drawings and specifications. </p><p>5.3. Payments must be made within 15 days of receiving an invoice, and payment delay will cause a direct delay to the project delivery.</p><p>5.4 Submittals Procedures:</p><p><br></p><p class="rt-in1">SPACE WORK shall prepare and submit deliverables to the Client for approval every 28 days, aligning with the specified milestones.</p><p class="rt-in1">The Client is entitled to review each submission up to two times, with each review period not exceeding seven (7) days. In case of rejection, SPACE WORK shall revise and resubmit within fourteen (14) days.</p><p class="rt-in1">If the Client fails to provide feedback within seven (7) days; failure to respond within (7) days submission shall be deemed approved, and SPACE WORK shall be entitled to invoice for the completed work.</p><p class="rt-in1">SPACE WORK reserves the right to reprice the work, within reasonable limits, based on the original contract pricing structure, should substantial revisions be required beyond the agreed-upon scope.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>5. Intellectual Property</strong> </p><p>6.1. All designs, drawings, and specifications provided by SPACEWORK remain its intellectual property until full payment is received. </p><p>6.2. Upon full payment, the Client receives a non-exclusive license to use the deliverables solely for the specified project. </p><p>6.3. SPACEWORK retains the right to use the designs for promotional and portfolio purposes.</p><p><strong>7. Confidentiality</strong> </p><p>7.1. Both parties agree to keep all project-related information confidential and not disclose it to any third party without prior written consent, except as required by law.</p><p><strong>8. Liability and Warranty</strong> </p><p>8.1. SPACEWORK will perform its services with professional care and diligence. </p><p>8.2. SPACEWORK is not liable for any project delays or costs arising from factors beyond its control, including Client-provided information or third-party dependencies. </p><p>8.3. The Client acknowledges that the deliverables are conceptual and may require further detailing and adjustment by third parties during execution.</p><p><strong>9. Termination</strong> </p><p>9.1. Either party may not terminate this Agreement, unless agreed by both parties. </p><p>9.2. Upon termination, the Client will compensate SPACEWORK for all work completed up to the termination date.</p><p><strong>10. Dispute Resolution</strong> </p><p>10.1. Any disputes arising from this Agreement will be resolved amicably through negotiations. </p><p>10.2. If negotiations fail, disputes will be subject to arbitration under the Rules of Conciliation and Arbitration at the Beirut Chamber of Commerce and Industry by three (3) Arbitrators appointed in accordance with the said rules. The said arbitrators shall have full power to open up, review and revise any decision, opinion, instruction, determination, certificate or valuation of the Engineer related to the dispute.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>11. Governing Law</strong> </p><p>This Agreement is governed by the laws of Lebanon.</p><p><strong>12. Entire Agreement</strong> </p><p>This Agreement constitutes the entire understanding between the parties and supersedes all prior agreements, understandings, or representations.</p><p><strong>13. Amendments</strong> </p><p>This Agreement may only be amended in writing and signed by both parties.</p><p><strong>IN WITNESS WHEREOF</strong>, the parties have executed this Agreement as of the date first written above.</p><p><strong>For SPACEWORK SARL</strong>                </p><p><strong>Kevin J. Gemayel</strong></p><p><em>Managing Director</em><br></p>'
 where company_id = (select id from public.companies where name = 'Space Work S.A.R.L')
   and name = 'Facade Architectural Services';

