ansfer fees. </p><p>5.2. Payment milestones are as follows: </p><p class="rt-in1">a. 25% upon signing this Agreement. </p><p class="rt-in1">b. 25% upon submission of Materials and systems</p><p class="rt-in1">c. 20% upon submission of specifications</p><p class="rt-in1">d. 20% upon submission of Facade General Drawings</p><p class="rt-in1">e. 10% Remaining balance upon delivery of final drawings and specifications. </p><p><br></p><p>5.3. Payments must be made within 15 days of receiving an invoice, and payment delay will cause a direct delay to the project delivery.</p><p>5.4 <u>Submital Procedures:</u></p><p>SPACE WORK shall prepare and submit deliverables to the Client for approval every 28 days, aligning with the specified milestones.</p><p>The Client is entitled to review each submission up to two times, with each review period not exceeding seven (7) days. In case of rejection, SPACE WORK shall revise and resubmit within fourteen (14) days.</p><p>If the Client fails to provide feedback within seven (7) days; failure to respond within (7) days submission shall be deemed approved, and SPACE WORK shall be entitled to invoice for the completed work.</p><p>SPACE WORK reserves the right to reprice the work, within reasonable limits, based on the original contract pricing structure, should substantial revisions be required beyond the agreed-upon scope.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>5. Intellectual Property</strong> </p><p>6.1. All designs, drawings, and specifications provided by SPACEWORK remain its intellectual property until full payment is received. </p><p>6.2. Upon full payment, the Client receives a non-exclusive license to use the deliverables solely for the specified project. </p><p>6.3. SPACEWORK retains the right to use the designs for promotional and portfolio purposes.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>7. Confidentiality</strong> </p><p>7.1. Both parties agree to keep all project-related information confidential and not disclose it to any third party without prior written consent, except as required by law.</p><p><strong>8. Liability and Warranty</strong> </p><p>8.1. SPACEWORK will perform its services with professional care and diligence. </p><p>8.2. SPACEWORK is not liable for any project delays or costs arising from factors beyond its control, including Client-provided information or third-party dependencies. </p><p>8.3. The Client acknowledges that the deliverables are conceptual and may require further detailing and adjustment by third parties during execution.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>9. Termination</strong> </p><p>9.1. Either party may not terminate this Agreement, unless agreed by both parties. </p><p>9.2. Upon termination, the Client will compensate SPACEWORK for all work completed up to the termination date.</p><p><strong>10. Dispute Resolution</strong> </p><p>10.1. Any disputes arising from this Agreement will be resolved amicably through negotiations. </p><p>10.2. If negotiations fail, disputes will be subject to arbitration under the Rules of Conciliation and Arbitration at the Beirut Chamber of Commerce and Industry by three (3) Arbitrators appointed in accordance with the said rules. The said arbitrators shall have full power to open up, review and revise any decision, opinion, instruction, determination, certificate or valuation of the Engineer related to the dispute.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>11. Governing Law</strong> </p><p>This Agreement is governed by the laws of Lebanon.</p><p><strong>12. Entire Agreement</strong> </p><p>This Agreement constitutes the entire understanding between the parties and supersedes all prior agreements, understandings, or representations.</p><p><strong>13. Amendments</strong> </p><p>This Agreement may only be amended in writing and signed by both parties.</p><p><strong>IN WITNESS WHEREOF</strong>, the parties have executed this Agreement as of the date first written above.</p><p><strong>For SPACEWORK SARL</strong>                </p><p><strong>Kevin J. Gemayel</strong></p><p><em>Managing Director</em><br></p>'
