-- INV/2026/00003
update public.invoices set narration = '<p><strong>SPACE WORK SARL</strong> (hereinafter referred to as “SPACEWORK”), a company duly registered under the laws of Lebanon, with its principal place of business located in Beirut, specializing in façade consulting, engineering, and design.</p><h2 class="rt-in1"><strong>1. Scope of Work</strong></h2><p>All mentioned works in the above BOQ for Sonam - Dakar project except the following exclusions:</p><p>1. Full façade shop drawings, Fabrication drawings, Installation drawings, Stamped structural calculations, Glass structural calculations, Laboratory testing fees, Site supervision, Authority submission and approval responsibility, Travel and accommodation,Redesign due to architectural, structural, client, authority, or contractor changes.</p><h2 class="rt-in1"><strong>2. Payment Terms and Milestones</strong></h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Milestone</th><th>Description</th><th>Percentage</th><th>Amount USD</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Advance
  payment upon appointment / contract signature</td><td>25%</td><td>2,500</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Completion
  of concept drawing / material submittal review round</td><td>25%</td><td>2,500</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Completion
  of material submittal</td><td>25%</td><td>2,500</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Submission
  of façade technical specification and recommendations</td><td>25%</td><td>2,500</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 class="rt-in1"><strong>3. Responsibilities of the Client</strong></h2><p>Provide SPACEWORK with all relevant project information, including architectural/structural drawings, conceptual façade package, project schedule, and design requirements. Provide timely decisions, approvals, and consolidated feedback. Appoint a single point of contact authorized to confirm decisions. Ensure all third-party design inputs (architect/structural/MEP) are coordinated and issued in current revision.</p><h2 class="rt-in1"><strong>4. Timeline</strong></h2><p>SPACEWORK will issue deliverables within a mutually agreed time frame starting from receipt of complete project information and formal appointment.  Delays caused by missing information, late approvals, or late feedback will result in corresponding extensions to the timeline and may result in additional fees if the delay exceeds <strong>thirty (30) calendar days</strong>.</p><h2 class="rt-in1"><strong>5. Fees and Payment Terms</strong></h2><p>5.1. All invoices shall be paid within 7 calendar days from invoice date.</p><p>5.2. Work on each milestone may be paused if the corresponding payment is delayed.</p><p>5.3. Any bank charges, transfer fees, or withholding taxes shall be borne by the Client.</p><p>5.4. Payments shall be made in fresh USD by bank transfer or cash payment, as agreed between parties.</p><h2 class="rt-in1"><strong>6. Submittal and Review Procedure</strong></h2><p>6.1. SPACEWORK shall submit deliverables to the Client based on the milestones above (or every <strong>28 days</strong> if the program requires phased submissions).</p><p>6.2. The Client is entitled to <strong>two (2) review cycles</strong> per submission, each review period not exceeding <strong>seven (7) days</strong>.</p><p>6.3. In case of rejection, SPACEWORK shall revise and resubmit within <strong>fourteen (14) days</strong>, subject to timely receipt of consolidated comments.</p><p>6.4. If the Client fails to provide feedback within <strong>seven (7) days</strong> of submission, the submission shall be deemed approved for invoicing purposes, and SPACEWORK shall be entitled to invoice for the completed milestone.</p><p>6.5. Requests that constitute <strong>scope expansion</strong> (e.g., moving to shop drawing/fabrication level, extensive redesign, additional façade areas/zones not included in the concept) may be repriced by SPACEWORK based on the original pricing structure and level of effort.</p><h2 class="rt-in1"><strong>7. Confidentiality</strong></h2><p>7.1. Both parties agree to keep all project-related information confidential and not disclose it to any third party without prior written consent, except as required by law.</p><h2 class="rt-in1"><strong>8. Liability and Warranty</strong></h2><p>8.1. SPACEWORK will perform its services with professional care and diligence.</p><p>8.2. SPACEWORK is not liable for delays or costs arising from factors beyond its control, including Client-provided information or third-party dependencies.</p><p>8.3. The Client acknowledges that the deliverables are <strong>implementation/tender-level</strong> and may require further detailing and development by a façade contractor/specialist during execution and shop drawing stages.</p><h2 class="rt-in1"><strong>9. Termination</strong></h2><p>9.1. Either party may terminate this Agreement only by mutual written agreement.</p><p>9.2. Upon termination, the Client will compensate SPACEWORK for all work completed up to the termination date.</p><h2><strong>10. Intellectual Property</strong></h2><p>10.1. All designs, drawings, and documents provided by SPACEWORK remain its intellectual property until full payment is received.</p><p>10.2. Upon full payment, the Client receives a non-exclusive license to use the deliverables solely for the Project.</p><p>10.3. SPACEWORK retains the right to use non-confidential visuals for portfolio and promotional purposes.</p><h2 class="rt-in1"><strong>11. Governing Law</strong></h2><p>This Agreement is governed by the laws of Lebanon.</p><h2 class="rt-in1"><strong>12. Entire Agreement</strong></h2><p>This Agreement constitutes the entire understanding between the parties and supersedes all prior agreements, understandings, or representations.</p><h2 class="rt-in1"><strong>13. Amendments</strong></h2><p>This Agreement may only be amended in writing and signed by both parties.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>IN WITNESS WHEREOF</strong>, the parties have executed this Agreement as of the date first written above.</p><p>For <strong>SPACEWORK SARL</strong></p><p><strong>Kevin J. Gemayel</strong></p><p>Managing Director</p>'
 where company_id = (select id from public.companies where name = 'Space Work S.A.R.L')
   and number = 'INV/2026/00003';

